{#- The homepage's header, on the desk above the mat (layouts/base.njk includes it
    when a page sets `hero:`): the line in a large italic outlined in the desk's
    grey, a sentence under it, and three photos of the work as prints with
    their captions written on. It is as wide as the mat and centred, so it
    lines up with the keys above and the mat below. Nothing here sits on the
    grid: the grid starts with the mat. -#}
<header class="home-hero">
  <h1 class="home-hero__line">Researcher,<br>Analyst &amp; Designer</h1>
  <p class="home-hero__sub">If it challenges assumptions, connects disciplines &amp; helps humans live better, I'm probably already thinking about it :)</p>
  <div class="home-hero__photos">
    {%- for photo in [
      { src: "/assets/images/home/polaroid-focus-group.jpg", alt: "People sitting on benches under trees in a focus group discussion", caption: "Focus group discussions at a partner hospital." },
      { src: "/assets/images/home/polaroid-ideo-launch.jpg", alt: "A room of people standing around a table beside a screen at an event", caption: "At the IDEO launch of the Financial Confidence Playbook." },
      { src: "/assets/images/home/polaroid-crown-paints.jpg", alt: "A woman in a denim jacket holding a green swatch book in front of a wall of paint colour cards", caption: "At Crown Paints trying to match the green in my hands." }
    ] %}
    <figure class="frame frame--polaroid"><img src="{{ photo.src }}" alt="{{ photo.alt }}" sizes="(max-width: 720px) 40vw, 210px" loading="eager"><figcaption>{{ photo.caption }}</figcaption></figure>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</header>
